  only is Luffy forever indebted to Shanks  for this but after receiving shank's  signature Straw Hat as a gift to  remember him by Luffy decided to follow  in his Idol's footsteps to lead a pirate  crew himself Luffy and Shanks promise to  reunite someday always just missing each  other over the course of one piece with  red continuing this narrative tradition  despite the two ostensibly working  together though Luffy and Shanks lead  their respective pirate Crews to work  together to stop utta and Destroy taught  musica the two captains don't actually  encounter each other over the course of  red this largely has to do with the  dimensional separation stemming from the  dream world with Luffy inside of the  dream world to confront tot musica while  Shanks remains elsewhere as Shanks and  his crew depart from eligia Island at  the end of the film he still hasn't  reunited with Luffy to see how far the  boy he saved has come as a pirate in his  own right with the promise unfulfilled  Luffy and Shanks still have unfinished  business between them to eventually  resolve  film red does include a post-credits  scene that shows Luffy back on his  pirate ship sailing away from elegia  Island for new adventures as he  contemplates his recent experiences just  as determined as ever Luffy declares to  the Open Sea that he will one day become  the king of the Pirates a lifelong  ambition he has maintained since  childhood red offers more insight into  Luffy's long-standing dream with his  adventure with utta reaffirming why he  intends to seize this position among the  pirate community in the New World by the  end of the film after reconciling with  her father and seeing the error of her  ways utta expresses her confidence in  Luffy one day achieving his dream the  esteemed role in the pirate Community  has remained vacant since the passing of  shank's Mentor gold D Roger leading  various pirate captains to bicker  amongst themselves for the title now  with a vote of confidence from his  childhood friend Luffy is more  determined than ever to finally become  king of the Pirates  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

